<%- include('partials/head', { pageTitle: "About — Climate Solutions" }) %>

<section class="bg-surface border-b border-rule">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl">About this project</h1>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 flex flex-col gap-10">

  <div>
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl">What it does</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
      This site catalogues climate solutions and groups them by the sector they act on,
      so you can look at one part of the economy at a time. Each entry describes the
      solution, what effect it has, and links out to the original research.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl">How it is built</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
      A Node.js and Express application rendering EJS templates on the server. Solutions
      and sectors live in a PostgreSQL database, accessed through Sequelize, with the two
      tables joined so every solution carries its sector. Adding, editing and deleting
      entries sits behind a session-based login, and the whole thing runs on Vercel.
    </p>
    <dl class="mt-6 border-t border-rule text-sm">
      <div class="flex gap-4 py-2.5 border-b border-rule">
        <dt class="w-32 shrink-0 text-muted">Server</dt>
        <dd>Node.js, Express</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4 py-2.5 border-b border-rule">
        <dt class="w-32 shrink-0 text-muted">Templating</dt>
        <dd>EJS</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4 py-2.5 border-b border-rule">
        <dt class="w-32 shrink-0 text-muted">Data</dt>
        <dd>PostgreSQL, Sequelize</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4 py-2.5 border-b border-rule">
        <dt class="w-32 shrink-0 text-muted">Styling</dt>
        <dd>Tailwind CSS</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4 py-2.5 border-b border-rule">
        <dt class="w-32 shrink-0 text-muted">Hosting</dt>
        <dd>Vercel</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl">Who built it</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
      Moustafa Elkerdany, a Computer Programming student at Seneca Polytechnic. I work
      mostly in JavaScript, Python and C++, and I am interested in Linux, cloud and
      networking.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <a href="https://github.com/mkerdany8" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-quiet">GitHub</a>
      <a href="mailto:mkerdany8@gmail.com" class="btn-quiet">Email</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl">Sources</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
      Solution descriptions and imagery come from
      <a href="https://drawdown.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-leaf underline underline-offset-2">Project Drawdown</a>,
      a non-profit that reviews and ranks climate solutions by the emissions they avoid.
    </p>
  </div>

</section>

<%- include('partials/foot') %>
